# Root build context hygiene.
#
# The http-ingress image is built from the REPO ROOT rather than from
# services/http-ingress, because it must contain schemas/event-ingest.schema.json
# (the ingress reads that file at runtime — docs/event-schema.md). A build context
# cannot reference a sibling directory, so the root is the only option.
#
# Consequence: without this file, every build uploads node_modules for all five
# services, the whole git history, and the docs. That is slow, and stale modules
# inside the context can shadow the ones the Dockerfile installs.
#
# Only these paths are actually needed by the Dockerfiles:
#   services/<svc>/package.json, services/<svc>/src, schemas/

node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# VCS and CI
.git/
.github/

# Local state and secrets
.env
.env.*
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Not needed to build any image
docs/
k8s/
scripts/
AGENTS.md
README.md
LICENSE

# Build output
**/dist/
**/coverage/
.DS_Store
